<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umar al-Aqta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 863</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Umar al-Aqta was emir of Melitene, a frontier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, from about 830 to 863 and one of the most dangerous Arab raiders of Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. Allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paulicians">Paulicians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divrigi">Tephrike</a>, he sacked Amisos on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> in 863, but was trapped and killed that year by a Byzantine army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petronas">Petronas</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lalakaon">Battle of Lalakaon</a>.</p></div>
